WEBVTT

00:01.170 --> 00:02.859
ARCANTEZ CASTLE

00:03.469 --> 00:03.826
Well then, here's to our alliance.

00:03.827 --> 00:05.637
Well then, here's to our alliance.
SEITZ ARMY'S OBJECTIVE

00:05.638 --> 00:06.304
SEITZ ARMY'S OBJECTIVE

00:06.305 --> 00:07.104
SEITZ ARMY'S OBJECTIVE
And to the new Duke of Seitz.

00:07.105 --> 00:09.433
And to the new Duke of Seitz.

00:09.889 --> 00:10.966
SEITZ DUKE
GRENDA DOMATSON

00:10.967 --> 00:12.895
I'm still not used to being called Duke.

00:14.104 --> 00:16.314
VASMARQUE SALEMAKHIA
Unlike your predecessor,

00:16.315 --> 00:19.235
I'm grateful you've allied with us.

00:19.777 --> 00:24.698
I hope to stay on good terms
with you, Missian's next Duke.

00:25.324 --> 00:27.576
We want the same things.

00:28.077 --> 00:30.162
As for your proposal,
Prince Vasmarque,

00:30.329 --> 00:34.124
you have Seitz's full cooperation.

00:34.416 --> 00:37.711
Our goal is to separate Canarre
from the main army.

00:38.626 --> 00:42.255
Their forces are far too strong
for a single county.

00:42.967 --> 00:45.344
I need your men to hold them back.

00:52.434 --> 00:53.806
Meet Boroths, my trusted right hand.

00:53.807 --> 00:54.669
Meet Boroths, my trusted right hand.
BOROTHS HEIGAND

00:54.670 --> 00:55.019
BOROTHS HEIGAND

00:55.020 --> 00:57.605
BOROTHS HEIGAND
He commanded our forces in the recent civil war.

00:57.606 --> 00:57.897
BOROTHS HEIGAND

00:57.898 --> 00:59.733
It's an honor to meet you.

01:00.734 --> 01:03.654
He will lead our attack on Canarre.

01:04.071 --> 01:07.283
We'll deploy an army of 80,000.

01:07.700 --> 01:09.785
You're certainly well prepared.

01:10.286 --> 01:12.371
An army ten times Canarre's size...

01:13.080 --> 01:17.084
There's something there
I intend to obtain at all costs.

01:19.003 --> 01:22.006
Our reward will be provisions
and resources,

01:22.965 --> 01:26.885
plus everything we seize
in Canarre, correct?

01:27.720 --> 01:29.346
Yes. Those are the terms.

01:30.055 --> 01:32.641
You're after their military power, right?

01:33.017 --> 01:34.268
Excuse me.

01:35.603 --> 01:38.355
Eager to start preparations, I see.

01:39.565 --> 01:40.816
May I ask you something?

01:41.900 --> 01:45.738
What will you do
once you're Duke of Missian?

01:46.030 --> 01:47.239
Declare independence?

01:48.782 --> 01:52.202
Couran is a pitiful man
who trusts no one.

01:53.120 --> 01:55.205
Not even his own family.

01:56.373 --> 01:59.543
I only wish to protect
my father's land and its people.

02:00.377 --> 02:01.378
That's all.

02:03.088 --> 02:05.341
Leave the fall of Canarre to us.

02:05.883 --> 02:09.553
You can focus on settling things
with your brother.

02:16.644 --> 02:20.481
Boroths. Gather troops
from all across Seitz.

02:20.939 --> 02:22.441
If I may, Your Grace...

02:23.150 --> 02:26.945
This war offers us little benefit.

02:28.322 --> 02:31.617
The land and provisions
offered are hardly substantial.

02:32.326 --> 02:34.036
We just emerged from a civil war.

02:34.286 --> 02:35.995
Could we not have demanded more?

02:35.996 --> 02:37.164
Listen, Boroths.

02:37.873 --> 02:40.668
Have you heard of Ars Louvent?

02:41.835 --> 02:43.754
Canarre's current Count? Yes. Why?

02:44.296 --> 02:46.465
He's only 13 years old.

02:46.715 --> 02:48.759
Don't you find that strange?

02:49.218 --> 02:53.806
They say he has a strange ability
to see people's talents.

02:54.348 --> 02:56.266
He can see... people's talents?

02:56.725 --> 03:01.188
I investigated him. His vassals
are indeed remarkably talented.

03:02.314 --> 03:04.608
I will take Canarre

03:04.775 --> 03:07.695
and bring Ars Louvent to my side.

03:08.487 --> 03:09.613
And you, Boroths,

03:09.905 --> 03:12.074
are one of my most trusted men.

03:12.700 --> 03:14.243
Don't let me down.

03:19.039 --> 03:20.582
Ars Louvent...

03:21.750 --> 03:24.128
What kind of man is he?

04:50.557 --> 04:54.666
As a Reincarnated Aristocrat, I'll Use My Appraisal Skill to Rise in the World Season 3

04:55.459 --> 04:56.469
EPISODE 26: CANARRE IN CRISIS

04:56.470 --> 04:59.046
EPISODE 26: CANARRE IN CRISIS
Lord Krall's letter reads as follows.

04:59.047 --> 04:59.469
EPISODE 26: CANARRE IN CRISIS

04:59.848 --> 05:03.101
Seitz is gathering troops near the Missian border.

05:03.310 --> 05:06.063
Their numbers are nearing 80,000.

05:06.605 --> 05:08.857
Immediate action is required.

05:09.525 --> 05:12.110
80,000...? Is that really possible?

05:12.444 --> 05:14.279
That's ten times Canarre's army.

05:15.239 --> 05:16.615
If those numbers are true,

05:17.074 --> 05:20.244
there's no way Coumeire alone
can stop their main army.

05:20.869 --> 05:23.163
Why Seitz again, though?

05:23.580 --> 05:26.375
Didn't they have a civil war
not long ago?

05:26.667 --> 05:27.709
That's correct.

05:28.585 --> 05:29.795
Some time ago,

05:30.045 --> 05:33.549
we signed a secret peace treaty
with Seitz amid the civil war.

05:34.132 --> 05:36.468
But during the unrest,

05:36.760 --> 05:39.054
a vassal ousted the former Duke.

05:39.513 --> 05:41.223
What you'd call a coup from below.

05:41.890 --> 05:44.017
So our treaty was probably discarded.

05:45.561 --> 05:47.354
But why attack now?

05:48.021 --> 05:51.733
They've barely restored order.
Things must still be chaotic.

05:52.234 --> 05:54.194
I've got a bad feeling about this.

05:55.195 --> 05:59.324
You were supposed to join
Prince Couran's army, right?

05:59.700 --> 06:00.742
Yes.

06:00.868 --> 06:03.996
This doesn't feel like a rash attack.

06:04.454 --> 06:06.081
Someone's pulling the strings.

06:07.958 --> 06:09.334
Sorry I'm late.

06:09.751 --> 06:12.754
Famme! What's the situation
with the Seitz forces?

06:13.922 --> 06:15.173
To put it simply...

06:15.757 --> 06:16.800
We're in trouble.

06:17.009 --> 06:18.719
I've never seen an army that big.

06:19.386 --> 06:20.846
Their commander is good, too.

06:21.263 --> 06:25.976
I hear he beat 100,000 troops
with only 50,000 in the civil war.

06:26.685 --> 06:27.728
Also...

06:28.562 --> 06:29.688
Is this...?

06:30.188 --> 06:31.899
A fire manastone...?

06:32.357 --> 06:33.441
It can't be!

06:33.442 --> 06:34.525
Yeah.

06:34.526 --> 06:37.821
Seitz doesn't produce
fire manastones naturally.

06:38.572 --> 06:40.908
That made me suspicious,
so I did some digging.

06:41.366 --> 06:42.409
And sure enough...

06:42.784 --> 06:45.120
At the same time Seitz began moving,

06:45.412 --> 06:48.373
Prince Vasmarque mobilized
his army toward Verzud.

06:48.749 --> 06:49.750
Just as I thought.

06:50.083 --> 06:54.588
Prince Vasmarque and Seitz's new Duke
must have formed an alliance.

06:55.255 --> 06:57.089
What? Is that bad?

06:57.090 --> 07:00.552
Prince Couran can't spare troops
to help us now.

07:01.678 --> 07:03.388
As things stand,

07:03.805 --> 07:06.308
we have to fight 80,000 Seitz troops.

07:07.601 --> 07:09.978
Are Canarre's defenses strong enough?

07:10.646 --> 07:12.356
Defense gives us an advantage, but

07:12.856 --> 07:15.359
our defensive facilities are limited.

07:16.818 --> 07:17.903
It would last...

07:18.070 --> 07:19.112
one year at best.

07:22.324 --> 07:24.242
At this rate, Canarre will fall.

07:24.952 --> 07:26.203
What can we possibly do?

07:27.537 --> 07:29.581
You could always defect.

07:32.918 --> 07:36.088
Naturally, they'd occupy Canarre
if you surrendered.

07:36.838 --> 07:39.967
But they might spare your life.

07:40.926 --> 07:43.387
Your Appraisal skill could earn you rank,

07:44.054 --> 07:45.973
and perhaps save your retainers too.

07:47.849 --> 07:48.976
I could never do that.

07:49.685 --> 07:52.020
Prince Couran entrusted Canarre to me,

07:52.270 --> 07:54.356
and I inherited it from Lumeire.

07:54.690 --> 07:55.774
And above all,

07:56.233 --> 07:57.943
it's the land my father protected.

07:58.944 --> 08:02.572
I serve as lord for one reason:
to protect my home.

08:03.323 --> 08:05.826
Giving it up without a fight is easy.

08:06.743 --> 08:10.330
But if the land is looted and ruined,
and the people suffer...

08:11.289 --> 08:14.084
That's exactly what
I've worked so hard to prevent.

08:15.293 --> 08:16.920
I refuse to choose that path.

08:17.796 --> 08:19.046
To me...

08:19.047 --> 08:21.258
and for those who protected Canarre,

08:22.217 --> 08:24.386
this is a battle we cannot lose.

08:27.305 --> 08:28.807
I knew you'd say that.

08:29.766 --> 08:33.270
From what I saw, they'll move
in a few weeks.

08:36.565 --> 08:39.234
Issue mobilization orders
throughout Canarre.

08:39.818 --> 08:40.819
One week from now,

08:41.111 --> 08:43.780
- we'll depart for Coumeire.
- Yes, my lord!

08:45.240 --> 08:48.243
Only months had passed
since House Louvent's new beginning.

08:48.785 --> 08:50.704
Its first true test has already come.

08:52.536 --> 08:54.536
A WEEK LATER

08:54.833 --> 08:55.959
Lord Ars!

08:56.418 --> 08:57.836
A letter from Prince Couran!

08:58.086 --> 08:59.087
And...

09:01.381 --> 09:02.883
I am aware of your situation.

09:03.759 --> 09:06.261
Canarre's defense is vital to us.

09:06.887 --> 09:09.973
I know this battle will be harsher
than anything you've faced,

09:10.098 --> 09:12.309
but I know you'll overcome it.

09:13.894 --> 09:17.147
You may not need them,
but I'm sending some troops.

09:17.647 --> 09:19.024
They're yours to command.

09:22.110 --> 09:24.821
Twenty thousand troops
from Prince Couran!

09:26.448 --> 09:27.449
Amazing...

09:30.660 --> 09:31.995
Oh! Clamant!

09:32.454 --> 09:33.955
It's the Maitlaw Mercenaries!

09:34.164 --> 09:36.041
This gives us a real fighting chance!

09:36.416 --> 09:39.669
Even with Vasmarque to fight,
Prince Couran still sent them...

09:40.128 --> 09:41.129
Lord Ars!

09:41.671 --> 09:44.174
Hammond Pleide,
Baron of Torbequista.

09:44.424 --> 09:47.010
I came as soon as I heard
of Canarre's crisis!

09:47.302 --> 09:48.428
Lord Hammond!

09:49.096 --> 09:50.097
Then there's...

09:52.766 --> 09:54.559
Here they are, kid.

09:55.060 --> 09:58.438
They're so fired up
they're driving me crazy.

10:00.649 --> 10:01.942
Acting Baron of Lamberg,

10:02.275 --> 10:03.527
Mireille Grandione.

10:03.944 --> 10:05.695
I came at my lord's command.

10:06.488 --> 10:10.450
It seems you're not the only one
who refuses to lose, Lord Ars.

10:12.536 --> 10:13.620
Right!

10:15.705 --> 10:16.790
Listen up!

10:16.915 --> 10:18.542
Thank you for fighting with us!

10:29.928 --> 10:31.596
Tell me, Rosell.

10:32.222 --> 10:35.725
How will 28,000 soldiers
beat an army of 80,000?

10:36.309 --> 10:38.645
We don't need to defeat them.

10:39.271 --> 10:40.647
What do you mean?

10:41.648 --> 10:43.775
Their army has fought nonstop.

10:44.317 --> 10:46.570
Their soldiers must be exhausted.

10:47.445 --> 10:51.074
And this is a war of invasion for them.

10:51.783 --> 10:55.245
Unlike their civil war,
this isn't a fight they must win.

10:56.246 --> 10:58.039
Which means their morale is weak!

10:59.749 --> 11:02.002
Given their alliance
with Prince Vasmarque,

11:02.377 --> 11:04.045
winning this battle

11:04.296 --> 11:06.423
must offer them some benefit.

11:07.257 --> 11:08.300
In that case,

11:08.508 --> 11:11.052
we make the war cost
more than it's worth.

11:12.137 --> 11:13.513
What we have to do

11:13.805 --> 11:16.099
isn't defeating all 80,000 troops.

11:16.808 --> 11:18.935
We must use our 28,000 wisely

11:19.311 --> 11:22.731
and make Seitz lose more
than it expects to gain,

11:23.064 --> 11:24.399
until they give up!

11:24.983 --> 11:26.193
For better or worse,

11:26.401 --> 11:28.987
simple numbers don't decide everything.

11:29.362 --> 11:31.448
That's what makes war interesting.

11:32.449 --> 11:33.575
Then our goal

11:33.783 --> 11:35.577
isn't about defeating the enemy,

11:35.952 --> 11:38.330
but to break their will to fight!

11:39.122 --> 11:41.750
We owe it to Prince Couran,
who sent us these troops,

11:41.917 --> 11:43.835
As a Reincarnated Aristocrat, I'll Use My Appraisal Skill to Rise in the World
let's make sure we win this!

11:45.629 --> 11:45.795
Wow!

11:45.796 --> 11:46.754
Wow!
As a Reincarnated Aristocrat, I'll Use My Appraisal Skill to Rise in the World

11:46.755 --> 11:47.454
As a Reincarnated Aristocrat, I'll Use My Appraisal Skill to Rise in the World

11:47.589 --> 11:49.799
- It's a perfect fit!
- It is!

11:52.344 --> 11:53.595
During this operation,

11:54.012 --> 11:55.889
I won't be able to stay by your side.

11:56.431 --> 11:57.724
So I hope that armor

11:58.183 --> 12:00.810
will protect you in my place.

12:02.020 --> 12:03.270
Thank you!

12:03.271 --> 12:04.356
Lord Ars!

12:05.732 --> 12:07.442
I have a gift for you too.

12:09.069 --> 12:10.320
Licia, what is this...?

12:10.779 --> 12:13.406
It's an extract of Lura leaves and petals.

12:14.074 --> 12:16.701
It's an old charm from Torbequista.

12:18.495 --> 12:20.163
They say if we embrace like this,

12:20.705 --> 12:23.083
you're certain to return safely.

12:24.417 --> 12:27.379
I thought Torbequista
charms only involved water...

12:28.004 --> 12:29.005
Anyway!

12:29.673 --> 12:31.132
While you're away, Lord Ars,

12:31.466 --> 12:33.301
I'll keep Canarre safe.

12:35.011 --> 12:36.263
See you when I return!

12:39.724 --> 12:41.017
Our battlefield this time

12:41.351 --> 12:44.562
is the Coumeire River
on the Missian-Seitz border.

12:45.272 --> 12:48.733
We've destroyed every bridge,
so they'll cross here.

12:49.651 --> 12:52.445
It is relatively narrow
and shallow in this area.

12:53.280 --> 12:55.782
It's the only place
80,000 troops can cross.

12:56.491 --> 13:00.829
Our main force of 20,000
will join Coumeire's army.

13:01.621 --> 13:05.125
We'll camp along the river
and stop their vanguard.

13:06.042 --> 13:08.962
The rest will hold Coumeire Fortress

13:09.296 --> 13:13.174
intercept flankers,
and support the main force.

13:16.094 --> 13:19.431
Rietz will have full command
of our main force.

13:20.991 --> 13:23.617
THE NIGHT BEFORE THE BATTLE

13:24.019 --> 13:26.521
You've done well to hold them this long.

13:27.772 --> 13:30.108
Defensive battles are my specialty.

13:30.442 --> 13:32.193
The real battle starts now.

13:32.736 --> 13:34.362
The terrain favors us.

13:34.946 --> 13:37.490
Your strategy is excellent as well.

13:41.119 --> 13:43.330
They'll reach
the Coumeire River tomorrow!

13:43.830 --> 13:46.166
Everyone, rest up for the battle!

13:46.916 --> 13:49.753
How am I supposed to sleep
before my first battle?

13:50.337 --> 13:53.214
Always inspect your weapons
before a battle begins.

13:54.716 --> 13:55.883
You got a letter.

13:55.884 --> 13:57.761
Oh, thank you.

14:01.765 --> 14:04.017
Why'd you become a vassal, Bro?

14:04.267 --> 14:06.393
Why do you wanna know?

14:06.394 --> 14:08.021
There's no special reason.

14:08.313 --> 14:11.648
Come on, you were famous long before this!

14:11.649 --> 14:14.652
The famous assault captain
of the Liben Company!

14:15.028 --> 14:17.072
Then you suddenly joined us.

14:17.364 --> 14:19.991
Is there some big dream behind it?!

14:20.658 --> 14:22.077
Money, I guess.

14:22.911 --> 14:23.953
Money...?

14:24.454 --> 14:28.750
I thought serving a noble
would make me rich.

14:29.292 --> 14:30.293
Whoa.

14:30.960 --> 14:32.420
Hey, guys.

14:32.545 --> 14:35.465
You won't get much sleep
once the fighting begins.

14:35.882 --> 14:38.468
Anyway, I'm going to bed.

14:39.052 --> 14:40.845
Charlotte's incredible.

14:41.262 --> 14:42.764
She's got nerves of steel.

14:43.473 --> 14:46.101
She's always been like that.

14:46.476 --> 14:48.436
She's built different from us.

14:51.731 --> 14:54.901
Dear Musia, as your mother,
I can't help worrying about you.

14:55.777 --> 14:58.613
Fighting just isn't in your nature.

14:59.364 --> 15:02.242
Maybe you got your clumsiness from me.

15:03.952 --> 15:07.330
You have lovely hair
and you're a beautiful girl.

15:07.705 --> 15:09.707
I'm sure you'll find a good husband.

15:10.875 --> 15:13.044
Leave the fighting to the men

15:13.628 --> 15:14.921
and come back home to us.

15:20.051 --> 15:21.261
I need to sleep.

15:22.406 --> 15:25.586
FEAR

15:29.644 --> 15:30.895
Miss Charlotte.

15:31.479 --> 15:34.149
Whoa! You scared me. Musia?

15:34.441 --> 15:35.859
You're not asleep yet?

15:36.317 --> 15:38.570
Just getting my weapon ready for tomorrow.

15:39.154 --> 15:41.156
I always do this before battle.

15:41.781 --> 15:44.701
You don't want bad gear
keeping you from fighting well.

15:45.285 --> 15:48.246
I'm going to bed soon,
so get some sleep, Musia.

15:48.830 --> 15:50.498
You'll collapse otherwise.

15:51.291 --> 15:52.292
Okay.

15:54.836 --> 15:56.045
Miss Charlotte,

15:56.337 --> 15:58.256
aren't you afraid of battle?

15:58.882 --> 15:59.924
I...

16:00.133 --> 16:03.470
I left home because I wanted
to stop being useless.

16:04.179 --> 16:06.473
I've given training everything I had.

16:06.848 --> 16:08.850
And yet... I'm scared.

16:09.767 --> 16:12.187
How can I make the fear go away?

16:14.355 --> 16:15.690
I'm scared too.

16:15.982 --> 16:17.232
Huh? But...

16:17.233 --> 16:19.402
Well, I'm not afraid of dying.

16:19.777 --> 16:20.945
I don't plan on losing.

16:21.196 --> 16:22.238
I see...

16:22.655 --> 16:25.992
I've spent most of my life fighting,
I've taken many lives.

16:26.993 --> 16:29.496
I live so I'll have no regrets
if I die tomorrow.

16:29.996 --> 16:31.331
That's not what scares me.

16:31.623 --> 16:32.957
What scares me is...

16:33.833 --> 16:35.627
letting Ars down.

16:37.712 --> 16:40.798
I want to change.
I want to believe in myself.

16:41.174 --> 16:43.718
I've always worried only about myself.

16:44.552 --> 16:46.304
But she's different.

16:47.180 --> 16:48.431
That's why she's strong.

16:49.307 --> 16:50.308
Um...

16:51.100 --> 16:52.602
Can I join you?

16:54.145 --> 16:56.147
Sure. I'll teach you.

16:57.398 --> 16:58.566
Maybe someday,

16:59.567 --> 17:00.902
I'll be like that too...

17:05.073 --> 17:07.366
Man, that snore is loud!

17:07.367 --> 17:10.244
Zaht, make him stop!

17:10.245 --> 17:12.455
There's no way we can sleep!

17:13.122 --> 17:14.165
Captain,

17:14.666 --> 17:15.875
could you keep it down?

17:17.919 --> 17:18.920
Brother...

17:20.046 --> 17:21.214
Dad...

17:23.800 --> 17:26.344
No wonder he can't sleep
hugging this thing.

17:26.594 --> 17:28.429
I'll put it away.

17:29.264 --> 17:30.682
Now we won't hear him.

17:30.932 --> 17:33.517
What? It's still just as loud!

17:33.518 --> 17:34.810
Come on, let's sleep.

17:34.811 --> 17:36.896
But our blankets are gone!

17:37.063 --> 17:38.106
Yeah, seriously!

17:40.390 --> 17:44.249
COUMEIRE RIVER

17:46.406 --> 17:48.991
ENEMY GENERAL RANTOLK ROODER
In Lord Boroths's name!

17:48.992 --> 17:50.368
Charge!

17:52.996 --> 17:54.789
Prevent the enemy from crossing.

17:54.998 --> 17:56.583
That is our mission.

17:57.834 --> 17:58.876
To Canarre,

17:59.210 --> 18:01.713
and to Lord Ars, bring victory!

18:02.422 --> 18:04.841
Ranged units, ready!

18:05.341 --> 18:06.384
Fire!

18:07.844 --> 18:10.138
Catapult units, forward!

18:14.392 --> 18:15.935
Heave!

18:21.232 --> 18:23.109
Mage unit! Defensive barrier!

18:30.408 --> 18:33.119
Vanguard! Advance!

18:35.538 --> 18:37.915
Ranged units, target the infantry!

18:44.380 --> 18:46.215
Their magic is stopping our fire!

18:46.591 --> 18:48.426
Keep attacking! Don't slow down!

18:49.552 --> 18:51.054
Charlotte! Musia!

18:51.846 --> 18:53.014
It's your turn.

18:54.057 --> 18:56.684
Finally, things are heating up.

18:57.685 --> 18:58.853
Begin the operation.

18:59.012 --> 19:00.809
MUSIA'S RESOLVE
Sorry to put pressure on you,

19:00.980 --> 19:02.815
but this battle rests on us.

19:03.608 --> 19:04.651
Ready?

19:04.942 --> 19:05.985
Yes.

19:06.194 --> 19:07.236
I'll be okay.

19:07.779 --> 19:10.615
Everyone's lives depend on this.
I have to be okay!

19:11.491 --> 19:14.661
Can a village girl like me
really do this?

19:15.370 --> 19:17.080
I don't know my limits yet. But...

19:18.039 --> 19:19.499
I can do this!

19:20.958 --> 19:22.001
Forma!

19:28.675 --> 19:29.758
N-No...

19:29.759 --> 19:30.802
I can't...

19:31.844 --> 19:33.471
Something must be wrong.

19:34.097 --> 19:35.306
Because I...

19:35.556 --> 19:37.809
I've never been good at anything.

19:38.726 --> 19:39.769
So...

19:40.561 --> 19:41.604
That's why...

19:44.774 --> 19:46.734
Musia, I believe in you.

19:47.527 --> 19:49.278
You really do have power.

19:49.696 --> 19:51.489
Ars said so, and he's never wrong.

19:55.576 --> 19:56.661
Have faith.

19:59.664 --> 20:00.665
I want to...

20:01.374 --> 20:03.376
I want to be like you, Charlotte!

20:06.671 --> 20:08.673
Please, give me your knife!

20:10.425 --> 20:12.510
I still can't believe in myself.

20:13.344 --> 20:15.304
But someday, I want to.

20:15.763 --> 20:17.932
I want to be someone
I can truly believe in.

20:18.683 --> 20:19.684
That's why!

20:27.483 --> 20:31.446
For now, I'll believe in Charlotte,
who believes in me!

20:32.447 --> 20:33.489
Forma...

20:34.157 --> 20:35.158
Terra Acos...

20:35.992 --> 20:37.034
Magnis!

20:48.880 --> 20:49.881
What?!

20:52.592 --> 20:53.676
The water?!

20:53.885 --> 20:56.179
Ranged units, fire!

20:56.429 --> 20:57.555
Forma...

20:57.889 --> 20:58.931
Igni...

20:59.098 --> 21:00.391
Erupt!

21:00.558 --> 21:01.893
Now's the chance!

21:02.059 --> 21:03.936
Charge with everything we've got!

21:11.569 --> 21:13.488
Finally, I get to fight!

21:13.780 --> 21:16.114
Zaht! Keep up with me!

21:16.115 --> 21:18.367
Don't charge too far ahead!

21:22.163 --> 21:23.414
Take this!

21:27.835 --> 21:30.004
Wh-What's happening...?

21:33.382 --> 21:35.343
R-Retreat!

21:46.771 --> 21:47.814
You did it!

21:53.486 --> 21:54.529
Yes!

23:26.210 --> 23:27.467
What do you think, Rietz?

23:27.468 --> 23:29.374
Our Musha is amazing, isn't she?

23:29.375 --> 23:32.100
Yeah, she is. And unlike
someone I know, she's a good girl.

23:32.101 --> 23:34.405
What did you say?! I'm a good girl too!

23:34.406 --> 23:36.725
Anyway, they're up next.

23:37.124 --> 23:37.712
Next time: "Zath and Braham"

23:37.713 --> 23:38.871
Next time: "Zath and Braham"
NEXT EPISODE: ZAHT AND BRAHAM

23:38.872 --> 23:39.900
NEXT EPISODE: ZAHT AND BRAHAM
